WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.320
Bend one hair on a mouse's back.

2
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.060
How many kinds of touch neuron can answer?

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:09.940
It depends on the hair.

4
00:00:10.883 --> 00:00:16.263
Mouse trunk skin has three main hair types: long guard hairs, awl/auchene hairs, and

5
00:00:16.263 --> 00:00:17.603
short, bent zigzag hairs.

6
00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:22.417
For decades, touch classes in hairy skin were defined by recording.

7
00:00:23.357 --> 00:00:25.357
The ending behind each was only inferred.

8
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.490
What changed was genetic access.

9
00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:33.770
A Cre driver mouse, crossed to a reporter, marks cells that expressed one chosen

10
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:34.770
gene.

11
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:40.270
But a label is only a handle, until recording confirms what the labelled neurons do.

12
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.970
Li and colleagues, in 2011, did that check.

13
00:00:44.933 --> 00:00:49.153
Neurons labelled by TrkB behaved as Aδ-LTMRs.

14
00:00:50.053 --> 00:00:51.913
They answer the tiniest hair deflections.

15
00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:56.517
Neurons with C-LTMR properties stained for TH.

16
00:00:57.777 --> 00:00:59.197
Slow, with intermediate adaptation.

17
00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.540
A third label, for some early Ret-expressing neurons, picked out Aβ beta R -A -L -T

18
00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.600
-M -R -S, Fast, and rapidly adapting.

19
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:13.843
Then they imaged whole sheets of trunk skin, to see which follicles each label

20
00:01:13.843 --> 00:01:14.843
surrounded.

21
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:17.853
Now bend an awl/auchene hair and hold it.

22
00:01:18.473 --> 00:01:19.733
Which labelled classes answer?

23
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:32.757
Three classes can: Aβ beta RA, Aδ delta, and C. Their lanceolate endings fence the

24
00:01:32.757 --> 00:01:33.757
same follicle.

25
00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:38.770
Each ending runs lengthwise along the follicle, like one picket in a fence.

26
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:44.410
Most awl/auchene and zigzag follicles also have circumferential endings from

27
00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:47.790
field-LTMRs, which Li did not label.

28
00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.950
That makes four classes at an awl/auchene follicle, and three at a zigzag one.

29
00:01:53.933 --> 00:01:58.413
Guard hairs carry Aβ beta RA endings, and a touch dome beside the hair.

30
00:01:59.293 --> 00:02:00.953
Zigzag hairs carry Aδ delta and C.

31
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:04.337
These combinations repeat across the skin.

32
00:02:05.237 --> 00:02:09.637
One movement of an awl/auchene hair can be reported by three classes in parallel.

33
00:02:10.717 --> 00:02:14.897
Assume their spikes start together and travel equal paths of 2 centimetres.

34
00:02:16.077 --> 00:02:18.337
Conduction alone gives these arrival times.

35
00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:23.490
The Aβ beta and Aδ delta reports arrive about 2 milliseconds apart.

36
00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:27.230
The C report arrives about 30 milliseconds later.

37
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.210
During the hold, the two rapid classes fall quiet.

38
00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.010
The C unit keeps firing for part of it.

39
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.070
On longer paths, every gap grows.

40
00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.810
What fires, and when its spikes arrive, both shape what the spinal cord receives.

41
00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.800
One caution. A single neuron branches to many hairs.

42
00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.040
So endings at a hair are not a count of neurons.

43
00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.480
One hair, three classes, three speeds.

44
00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:57.940
The skin splits even a single hair movement into parallel reports.
